  "content": "<p><strong>Note this page is for DevOps team. </strong>Paste markdown below as Team message in GitHub. Don&rsquo;t forget to replace project name to current value e.g. CWCalc.</p><p>Title: Welcome to Inter IKEA GitHub!</p><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"1cf0020f-8e3d-4e5f-b38b-9502bf4946fe\"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[# IPEX DevOps setup\n\nMembers in this team has been onboarded to IPEX DevOps setup where GitHub is one key part. New members of the team would typically be added to team by your PO/SO. Besides GitHub you as well have access to an Azure DevOps project and Azure subscription(s)\n\n## GitHub\n\nBeing a member of a team implies that you have Admin access for your teams repositories that you find by filtering on {project name} and that:\n\n- You are able to collaborate and make PR:s for [KOMPIS](https://github.com/inter-ikea/CBF-RE-IPEX-KOMPIS). \n- You can as well help out improve [default pipeline](https://github.com/inter-ikea/cbf-re-ipex-devops-setup-aoa-planner/tree/main/.github/workflows).\n- You have read access for all IPEX repositories. \n\nCurrently you have to notify IPEX DevOps team when you want [additional team repositories](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2252243047/Create+GitHub+repository).\nSome [GitHub Advanced Security](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2481356877/GitHub+Advanced+Security) features are enabled by default.\n\n## Azure DevOps\nAn [Azure DevOps project](https://dev.azure.com/iissab-ipex/) where you configure Azure Artifacts which is the way we share artifacts between products. To build your application it is recommeded that you use IPEX common feed so that we easily can build IPEX applications\n## Azure\nIf you used Azure - which is the preferred cloud platform - you find you [Azure subscriptions](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2891219032/Azure+subscriptions) in the [Azure Portal](https://portal.azure.com/) or if you prefer CLI the [Azure Cloud Shell](https://portal.azure.com/#cloudshell/) \nIt is the responsibility of the team to monitor cost and security for provisioned services.\n\n## Documentation\nYou can find more information at [IPEX Home wiki](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/1000013985/WAYS+OF+WORKING) about:\n\n- [IPEX DevOps setup](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2676621319/IPEX+DevOps+setup)\n- [Tooling](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/1176405288/Our+Tools)\n- [Cloud](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2500624806/Cloud)\n\n## Support\nFor any questions please contact the [IPEX DevOps team](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2316238888/IPEX+DevOps+team) or ask a question in the [DevOps Slack channel](https://i-p-e-x.slack.com/archives/C0273SG84TE).\n\n\nBest Regards\n\n/[IPEX DevOps Team](https://i-p-e-x.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IPEX/pages/2316238888/IPEX+DevOps+team)]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p />",
